     rationale: record.py represents process stats (94), process descriptions (153), disk results (216,245), search rules/classifications (337,348,404), findings (458), inventory groups (527), samples (584,623), failures (654), stopping results (684), prior summaries (723), and final reports (828–830) as positional tuples, heterogeneous dictionaries, or string statuses.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:94: Use a named process-stat model instead of a four-position tuple accessed by numeric indices.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:153-176: Process descriptions have a stable heterogeneous schema suited to a typed model.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:216: Disk measurements combine total, per-path usage, and duration in an unnamed positional tuple.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:245: Allocated-entry counts and bytes should use named result fields.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:337-345: Search rules use positional kind/regex pairs and string kinds instead of a typed rule model.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:348-401: Curated classifications use positional status/reason tuples and string statuses instead of typed classifications.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:404-433: Classification results return stringly typed status/reason tuples.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:458-466: Search findings have a stable schema but are constructed as heterogeneous dictionaries.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:525-547: Inventory groups and totals use mutable object-valued dictionaries requiring casts and suppressions instead of typed models.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:584-592: Disk samples use heterogeneous dictionaries instead of a typed sample model.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:623: Host samples use heterogeneous dictionaries instead of a typed sample model.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:649-655: Failed-test records encode node ID, reason, and subsequently added rerun result as bare dictionaries.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:684: Process-stopping outcomes use an object-valued dictionary with differently shaped lists instead of named typed fields.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:723-733: Prior-attempt records are reconstructed as untyped dictionaries rather than parsed into a summary model.
     spikes/gate-host-impact/record.py:828-882: Cleanup and the nested report schema are assembled as bare dictionaries and consumed through string keys; define typed report models before serialization.
